WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.624
Episode eight: a history-matching study.

2
00:00:02.624 --> 00:00:06.100
This video assumes APEX installed, as in episode one.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.051
Run every command below from the APEX folder.

4
00:00:09.051 --> 00:00:15.479
The case is the linear-Gaussian example of Your first history-matching run (episodes two to five).

5
00:00:15.479 --> 00:00:21.589
It runs in seconds and needs no reservoir simulator.

6
00:00:21.589 --> 00:00:33.183
A study runs every combination of cases, methods and variants, several times with different seeds (the replicates), and compares the results.

7
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:34.359
The example has one.

8
00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:54.355
[study]: its name (linear_methods), 3 replicates, the seed the later replicates' seeds come from (the first keeps the case's own), and the metrics to compare.

9
00:00:54.355 --> 00:01:06.193
[study.cases]: the case, the example's ES-MDA configuration.

10
00:01:06.193 --> 00:01:21.665
[study.methods.esmda] and [study.methods.gies]: each a complete [method] section.

11
00:01:21.665 --> 00:01:35.103
[[study.variants]]: a change to the case for every run, here an ensemble of 100 members instead of 500.

12
00:01:35.103 --> 00:01:36.385
Check its cost first.

13
00:01:36.385 --> 00:01:51.055
The plan ends with the study's total.

14
00:01:51.055 --> 00:02:02.033
Jobs submitted from the command line run a frozen copy of APEX's code by default, so that editing the APEX folder never changes a running job.

15
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:13.075
The first submission makes the copy, a git worktree of the commit with an environment of its own, which takes a few minutes and about 2 GB; uncommitted changes are not in it.

16
00:02:13.075 --> 00:02:17.806
Ours was made before this video.

17
00:02:17.806 --> 00:02:21.591
apex study run submits the 6 runs as background jobs.

18
00:02:21.591 --> 00:02:37.389
Without --wait it returns at once; with it, it waits and prints study complete.

19
00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:47.298
The runs go to the services root ($APEX_HOME, by default ~/.apex/service), in studies/linear_methods/.

20
00:02:47.298 --> 00:02:59.621
apex study status counts the runs by state (6 complete).

21
00:02:59.621 --> 00:03:14.071
And apex jobs list lists every job with its state.

22
00:03:14.071 --> 00:03:37.795
apex study compare gives each method's mean and spread over the replicates, and the paired difference with a Wilcoxon test.

23
00:03:37.795 --> 00:03:46.613
With 3 replicates the test cannot show a difference (compare says so); a real comparison needs more.

24
00:03:46.613 --> 00:03:56.059
apex study run takes the study file, while status and compare take the study's name, its [study] name.

25
00:03:56.059 --> 00:04:03.303
So: validate the study first, run it, follow it by its name, and compare the methods over the replicates.

26
00:04:03.303 --> 00:04:06.615
And remember: three replicates are only a start.

27
00:04:06.615 --> 00:04:13.248
Next, in episode nine: the job service from the terminal.

28
00:04:13.248 --> 00:04:18.748
Thank you for watching.
